From: Khem Raj <khem.raj@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 01:56:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] device: cast BLKGETSIZE64 ioctl request to int for musl

musl declares ioctl()'s request parameter as plain int, while
BLKGETSIZE64 expands (via _IOR/_IOC) to an expression that includes
sizeof(size_t), making its type unsigned long. Passing it directly
narrows an unsigned long to int and trips -Wsign-conversion under
-Werror. Only the low 32 bits of the request are meaningful to the
kernel ioctl syscall, so an explicit cast to int is safe and matches
common musl portability practice.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Khem Raj <khem.raj@oss.qualcomm.com>
---
--- a/src/device.cpp	2026-09-29 01:56:34.726173722 +0000
+++ b/src/device.cpp	2026-09-29 01:56:34.727037189 +0000
@@ -160,7 +160,7 @@
     if (::fstat(fd, &statbuf) != 0) {
         return 0;
     }
-    if (S_ISBLK(statbuf.st_mode) && (::ioctl(fd, BLKGETSIZE64, &size) != 0)) {
+    if (S_ISBLK(statbuf.st_mode) && (::ioctl(fd, static_cast<int>(BLKGETSIZE64), &size) != 0)) {
         return 0;
     }
 
